{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1271546-voice-of-the-angel-god-machine","id":1271546,"title":"Voice of the Angel (God-Machine)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-11-28T13:06:23-08:00","id":1271546,"title":"Voice of the Angel (God-Machine)","content":"So it is no secret that 2nd edition has a place within the universe for the God-Machine. My question is not if the God-Machine exists, but if the events that supposedly transpired such as in Voice of the Angel (1st edition core admittedly) came to pass. Granted they are two different editions, but I can easily see the story of the history of the world also apply towards 2nd edition unless additional information presents itself to contradict it.<br /> <br /> If the events did happen as told, where would you say Pangaea or the First Children come into play? Being that the Third Children also supposedly existed at this time essentially as immortals as well before the fall of the First Children, would it be fair to say humans also existed at the time of Pangaea and Father Wolf?<br /> <br /> Edit: Come to think of it...I wonder if the God-Machine had anything to do with the creation of spirits as well","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T13:20:33-08:00","id":1271551,"title":"","content":"In the Sundered World Dark Era, in Dark Eras, we see that the fall of Pangaea occurred at some point in the end of or after the Neolithic Age, which was about 5000 years ago. Humans existed at the same time, the Vinca peoples had settlements in what is now places like Serbia and Bulgaria.<br /> <br /> One of the big theories going around is that the God Machine is Great Mountain, one of the Pangaeans mentioned in this Dark Era, known for gathering people to build things.<br /> <br /> A lot is going to depend on how you see the God Machine. I've never thought of it as something that was before time and has existed since, as much as an entity that created at some point and in order to keep it from being un-created then established itself in other times retroactively.<br /> <br /> Based on the whole 'other peoples gods are demons' point of view a lot of religions bring to the table, as well as the general demonization they face, the Pangaeans and their surviving descendants may be the Second Children.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-28-2018, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T13:47:08-08:00","id":1271566,"title":"","content":"That said, it must be noted that Marco Singe is very much insane, and therefore it's a question how much of what he said is actually based on anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T13:50:45-08:00","id":1271568,"title":"","content":"Absolutely. Between his own insanity and angels not exactly being required to tell the truth pretty much everything's up in the air.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T14:11:18-08:00","id":1271573,"title":"","content":"Apparently I need to read Dark Eras since I have not gotten around to them yet. I always assumed probably incorrectly that those books were mostly plot setting books rather than greater lore. Or was my assumption correct?<br /> <br /> Regardless, even if Marco is insane and the the angels not being required to tell the truth, it is still an interesting piece of story lore that I felt really captured the World of Darkness feeling.<br /> <br /> As for the God-Machine itself, since I am not running a Demon game, I am trying to find ways to incorporate it without going into infrastructure and the like. My feeling at this moment in time is to treat it as an abstract entity as limited or as powerful as it needs to be within the scope of the story, but definitely needing to keep it consistent so it doesn\u2019t become seen as a McGuffin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T14:23:51-08:00","id":1271580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1271546-voice-of-the-angel-god-machine?p=1271573#post1271573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apparently I need to read Dark Eras since I have not gotten around to them yet. I always assumed probably incorrectly that those books were mostly plot setting books rather than greater lore. Or was my assumption correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are plot setting books but in many cases there's a lot of lore. For instance you see mages before Orders, werewolves in Pangaea before tribes were a thing, Promethean lineages that have since died out and so on.<br /> <br /> The Marco Singe testament definitely captures a lot of the essence of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T14:29:19-08:00","id":1271583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1271546-voice-of-the-angel-god-machine?p=1271551#post1271551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the big theories going around is that the God Machine is Great Mountain, one of the Pangaeans mentioned in this Dark Era, known for gathering people to build things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait- is that a thing? Never heard that theory before.<br /> <br /> And yeah, if you wish to introduce the God Machine into Forsaken's setting, using the Pangaeans as the Second Children is a good way to start- whatever relationship the old beast gods had with the Machine is up in the air, but I just can't see Father Wolf and the God Machine having friendly relationships. Bull, perhaps, Bird maybe- but Wolf? Far too different in character to work together. Perhaps Bird was the &quot;demon&quot; from the story which taught mankind the secrets of the Black Sun Map in exchange for the death brought by the atomic bombs, as Marco Singe claims? After all, the Perspective does have some weird interest in nuclear energy. Funny how things work out, ah?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T15:24:28-08:00","id":1271601,"title":"","content":"Well one of the hallmarks of a good story is how well it can be adapted to different needs depending on who the audience is. Reading it from a Hunter perspective vs a Werewolf perspective as an example produces two very different outcomes <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T17:32:03-08:00","id":1271633,"title":"","content":"Speaking of the GM, is it just assumed that the characters in the Corebook God-Machine Chronicle adventures are some sort of stigmatics, given that they are presumably seeing past concealment infrastructure in at least some of those chapters?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T17:40:52-08:00","id":1271635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1271546-voice-of-the-angel-god-machine?p=1271633#post1271633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of the GM, is it just assumed that the characters in the Corebook God-Machine Chronicle adventures are some sort of stigmatics, given that they are presumably seeing past concealment infrastructure in at least some of those chapters?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Most often, they cheat explicit concealment infrastructure by following the weirdness that it can't cover back in and through the Linchpin in some form or fashion.<br /> <br /> Like, they can't see past the perception filter that demons can inherently see through, but they can still notice when a man with a funny hat pops in and out of a wall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T17:56:15-08:00","id":1271640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1271546-voice-of-the-angel-god-machine?p=1271635#post1271635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. Most often, they cheat explicit concealment infrastructure by following the weirdness that it can't cover back in and through the Linchpin in some form or fashion.<br /> <br /> Like, they can't see past the perception filter that demons can inherently see through, but they can still notice when a man with a funny hat pops in and out of a wall.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean that doesn't happen in your day to day life?<br /> <br /> As it currently stands with the God-Machine I am trying to work into my chronicle and what caused me to even think of this post, I am treating it as in some way shape or form as being responsible for the fall of Father Wolf/Pangaea. For reasons only known to its' clockwork machinations, it required the energy/resonance/trauma from the shattering of the Border Marches into the separate worlds. Many decades/centuries/millenea of tiny events each leading to bigger and bigger events transpired before the pendulum finally swung and the Uratha tore out Father Wolf's throat.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T19:09:10-08:00","id":1271661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1271546-voice-of-the-angel-god-machine?p=1271640#post1271640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean that doesn't happen in your day to day life?<br /> <br /> As it currently stands with the God-Machine I am trying to work into my chronicle and what caused me to even think of this post, I am treating it as in some way shape or form as being responsible for the fall of Father Wolf/Pangaea. For reasons only known to its' clockwork machinations, it required the energy/resonance/trauma from the shattering of the Border Marches into the separate worlds. Many decades/centuries/millenea of tiny events each leading to bigger and bigger events transpired before the pendulum finally swung and the Uratha tore out Father Wolf's throat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, perfectly feasible.<br /> <br /> You've got some scale to work with, mind, depending on if you want to tip the balance at a critical moment or have it be a long standing plan come to fruition-the latter could easily see humanity's growth into agriculture that weakened Wolf to begin with. The former could incarnate any number of ways at tense tipping points where something <i>else</i> could have been done to revive the Great Predator-tying into Gilgamesh and a story that feels an awful lot like a God-Machine move*, maybe Snake was going to intervene before something happened to her.<br /> <br /> *The story of King Arthur and Mordred's final conflict has a moment where something other than their final conflict could have happpened, where they and their arrayed soldiers met on the battlefield to negotiate. Tensions are high as the two meet. The conversation starts and maybe, just maybe, something could have been reconciled....except, at that time, there was a snake that reared to strike the ankle of a soldier. Not that big of a deal, <i>except</i> a soldier drew their sword to cut it down, and in that scenario, one sword drawn in a sea of itchy knights basically sparked the whole shindig, and fate happens.<br /> <br /> The snake's involvement is totally a God-Machine move.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T03:40:38-08:00","id":1271733,"title":"","content":"Minimal effort, for maximum results.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T06:23:22-08:00","id":1271756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1271546-voice-of-the-angel-god-machine?p=1271573#post1271573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apparently I need to read Dark Eras since I have not gotten around to them yet. I always assumed probably incorrectly that those books were mostly plot setting books rather than greater lore. Or was my assumption correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sundered World is a bit unusual in this respect because it's set before the Sundering, and hence gives additional insight and material into the pre-Sundering situation.<br /> <br /> Some other Eras do have some overall setting lore additions featured, but it varies from Era to Era. Both of the Eras involving Forsaken that I've contributed to for Dark Eras 2, for example, will feature some lore-relevant content for the game, but both are quite ignorable without the setting particularly losing out.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T08:14:34-08:00","id":1271774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1271546-voice-of-the-angel-god-machine?p=1271566#post1271566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, it must be noted that Marco Singe is very much insane, and therefore it's a question how much of what he said is actually based on anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but like any (potential) Stigmatic, for every word of maddening ramble, there might be a glimpse of prophesy between them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T09:36:02-08:00","id":1271787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1271546-voice-of-the-angel-god-machine?p=1271756#post1271756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Sundered World is a bit unusual in this respect because it's set before the Sundering, and hence gives additional insight and material into the pre-Sundering situation.<br /> <br /> Some other Eras do have some overall setting lore additions featured, but it varies from Era to Era. Both of the Eras involving Forsaken that I've contributed to for Dark Eras 2, for example, will feature some lore-relevant content for the game, but both are quite ignorable without the setting particularly losing out.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's handy to know!<br /> <br /> What I would find interesting is if the God-Machine itself is actually a spirit itself, rank 9/10 potentially. We know at least according to lore (admittedly spoken by an insane man) is that it created the world and hence obviously has a significant inherent power, but is our assumption that it is a machine really accurate? Or is it simply how aeons of thought/feeling/conceptualization/universal construct have shaped it?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T11:13:11-08:00","id":1271800,"title":"","content":"the god machine created the world? I thought it merely wove intricate occult matrices into the fabric of our reality/world","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T11:24:22-08:00","id":1271802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1271546-voice-of-the-angel-god-machine?p=1271800#post1271800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the god machine created the world? I thought it merely wove intricate occult matrices into the fabric of our reality/world</div> </div> </div> </div>Likely it didn't, but its angel supposedly tells Marco that, and you can take them both on their word and what they say literally.<br /> <br /> 'The god-machine built our world as a resting place for its First Children, whom men called angels or Ancient Ones.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T11:36:01-08:00","id":1271808,"title":"","content":"hmm, that could also be interpreted as making the mortal realm able to house angels. I think the devs have even referred to the god machine as an invader","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T11:43:43-08:00","id":1271812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1271546-voice-of-the-angel-god-machine?p=1271808#post1271808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hmm, that could also be interpreted as making the mortal realm able to house angels. I think the devs have even referred to the god machine as an invader</div> </div> </div> </div>I should have posted the whole thing, here's just the 'creation of the world' part, there's significantly more, it's all in the original World of Darkness core and I believe it was reprinted in the God Machine Chronicle fiction anthology..<br /> <br /> 'The god-machine built our world as a resting place for its First Children, whom men called angels or Ancient Ones. After a time, the ancients desired servants to dwell with them, servants who walked upright and had pleasing shapes, and who could speak. They sent the proper prayer-signals to the god-machine and were granted leave to do so. First the Ancient Ones took the beasts of the field and granted them the knowledge to speak and walk. But these animals retained their wildness and did not make good servants. They grew wicked and violent, and were cast into the wilderness. They were the Second Children, whom men called demons.<br /> <br /> So the Ancients called new servants into being and commanded them to spread across the face of the Earth. And these were the Third Children, called mankind. And mankind served the ancients in peace and contentment. Mankind knew not death then. Those whose bodies became worn and aged were sent to sleep in the shadow of the Earth and returned after a time restored to health and youth.'<br /> <br /> It's the usual creation story. I don't think the God Machine is ever going to be statted out, it's not that type of entity. It gets a little bit into why it's called the God-Machine, but most of that is in Demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-29-2018, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T12:15:25-08:00","id":1271824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1271546-voice-of-the-angel-god-machine?p=1271787#post1271787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's handy to know!<br /> <br /> What I would find interesting is if the God-Machine itself is actually a spirit itself, rank 9/10 potentially. We know at least according to lore (admittedly spoken by an insane man) is that it created the world and hence obviously has a significant inherent power, but is our assumption that it is a machine really accurate? Or is it simply how aeons of thought/feeling/conceptualization/universal construct have shaped it?</div> </div> </div> </div>The God-Machine is the sum total of all the Infrastructure there is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-29-2018, 03:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T15:57:50-08:00","id":1271863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1271546-voice-of-the-angel-god-machine?p=1271824#post1271824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The God-Machine is the sum total of all the Infrastructure there is.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it is a circular cycle? The God-Machine creates the infrastructure and it in turn is the God-Machine?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T16:00:39-08:00","id":1271864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1271546-voice-of-the-angel-god-machine?p=1271863#post1271863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it is a circular cycle? The God-Machine creates the infrastructure and it in turn is the God-Machine?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. The God-machine is a self-perpetuating system first and foremost, which is why the two forefronts of horror with it are the maintenence of the status quo and the subsumption of individuals into it's mass.<br /> <br /> &quot;God be with you&quot; is a very rude thing to wish on people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T17:48:52-08:00","id":1271887,"title":"","content":"As far as we know, the only real truths in Voice of the Angel are that the God-Machine exists and that the moon landings were arranged to plunder some sort of crypt on the Moon, but a Storyteller could decide to say that some other aspects of it are true.<br /> <br /> As for me, I like to think of 'Voice of the Angel' primarily as the Deva Corporation's mythology regarding the God-Machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T08:37:32-08:00","id":1271983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1271546-voice-of-the-angel-god-machine?p=1271661#post1271661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, perfectly feasible.<br /> <br /> You've got some scale to work with, mind, depending on if you want to tip the balance at a critical moment or have it be a long standing plan come to fruition-the latter could easily see humanity's growth into agriculture that weakened Wolf to begin with. The former could incarnate any number of ways at tense tipping points where something <i>else</i> could have been done to revive the Great Predator-tying into Gilgamesh and a story that feels an awful lot like a God-Machine move*, maybe Snake was going to intervene before something happened to her.<br /> <br /> *The story of King Arthur and Mordred's final conflict has a moment where something other than their final conflict could have happpened, where they and their arrayed soldiers met on the battlefield to negotiate. Tensions are high as the two meet. The conversation starts and maybe, just maybe, something could have been reconciled....except, at that time, there was a snake that reared to strike the ankle of a soldier. Not that big of a deal, <i>except</i> a soldier drew their sword to cut it down, and in that scenario, one sword drawn in a sea of itchy knights basically sparked the whole shindig, and fate happens.<br /> <br /> The snake's involvement is totally a God-Machine move.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmm? Not a Snake move? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Snake is all about unexpected and sudden endings. Camelot is a LOT of infrastructure to go to waste--especially when Merlin ascends and Ruin smashes the corpse of Britain flat.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T13:18:43-08:00","id":1272031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1271546-voice-of-the-angel-god-machine?p=1271983#post1271983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Hmm? Not a Snake move? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Snake is all about unexpected and sudden endings. Camelot is a LOT of infrastructure to go to waste--especially when Merlin ascends and Ruin smashes the corpse of Britain flat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Within the context of the comparison it was made in(namely, comparing that moment to the God-Machine's involvement with the Third Reich), it is a God-Machine move.<br /> <br /> Besides, assuming that the God-Machine was involved in Camelot, one has to ask if that moment didn't fulfill both the God-Machine's and Merlin's purposes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T16:19:31-08:00","id":1272067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1271546-voice-of-the-angel-god-machine?p=1272031#post1272031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Within the context of the comparison it was made in(namely, comparing that moment to the God-Machine's involvement with the Third Reich), it is a God-Machine move.<br /> <br /> Besides, assuming that the God-Machine was involved in Camelot, one has to ask if that moment didn't fulfill both the God-Machine's and Merlin's purposes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Within that context, sure. And definitely a Merlin move. Dude was probably hanging in some astral realm at that moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T16:44:51-08:00","id":1272077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1271546-voice-of-the-angel-god-machine?p=1272067#post1272067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Within that context, sure. And definitely a Merlin move. Dude was probably hanging in some astral realm at that moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude was probably at his Cintamani, waiting for the Omen to fully come into being so he could Ascend his ass pronto when it did. Remember, the Fall of Camelot was what allowed Merlin to finish his Ascension.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T17:15:22-08:00","id":1272079,"title":"","content":"The God-Machine has been known to mess with timelines (see Seattle), and I wouldn't be a bit surprised to learn that it can participate in acts of Imperium. As well, God-Machine Chronicle has a bit in its discussion about Tiers where it hints that the God-Machine might have been behind the Fall of Atlantis (read the backstory of the Gnomes of Zurich with Mage in mind). It wouldn't surprise me in the least if the origins of the God-Machine lie in another timeline: it's not that It predates time, per se, so much as it comes from a Time Before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T17:28:08-08:00","id":1272081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1271546-voice-of-the-angel-god-machine?p=1272079#post1272079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The God-Machine has been known to mess with timelines (see Seattle), and I wouldn't be a bit surprised to learn that it can participate in acts of Imperium. As well, God-Machine Chronicle has a bit in its discussion about Tiers where it hints that the God-Machine might have been behind the Fall of Atlantis (read the backstory of the Gnomes of Zurich with Mage in mind). It wouldn't surprise me in the least if the origins of the God-Machine lie in another timeline: it's not that It predates time, per se, so much as it comes from a Time Before.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lodge of the Clocktower might explicitly exist because of this, bringing it all around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-28T19:16:32-08:00","id":1277294,"title":"","content":"Just as an update, the addition of the god-machine went over extremely well and has at least in the nature of my game (liberties have been taken), been the progenitor of the hosts itself. The god-machine for its arcane/unknown reasons, needed the separation of flesh and spirit and what better way than to warp and nudge some minor rat and spider entities to evolve in unexpected ways to eventually bring down the great wolf itself by nature of revealing his weakness to all his firstborn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}